"""
RoomSync network config — values that change depending on where things are
physically running, so they're kept out of app.py/rfid_listener.py.

This is a template. Copy it to config.py (which is gitignored — never
committed, never touched by git pull) and fill in the real values for
*this* machine. Every machine (laptop, Raspberry Pi) keeps its own
config.py with its own values.

SMS_GATEWAY_IP/SMS_GATEWAY_PORT: the spare Android phone's REST SMS
Gateway app. Match these to whatever that app currently displays on the
phone's screen, and restart `python app.py` after editing. Only matters
on whichever machine is actually running app.py. The machine running
app.py and that phone must be on the same WiFi network (or the phone's
own hotspot) for this to work at all — see CLAUDE.md's "SMS
Notifications" section.

ROOMSYNC_SERVER_URL: where rfid_listener.py POSTs each tap. Leave this as
the 127.0.0.1 default when app.py runs on the same machine as the RC522
reader (the normal Raspberry Pi setup). If app.py is instead running on a
laptop for a demo — RFID reader still on the Pi via rfid_listener.py, but
the display/admin pages shown on the laptop's bigger screen — change this
to the laptop's LAN IP (e.g. "http://192.168.1.23:5000") on the Pi's copy
of config.py. app.py itself doesn't read this value; only
rfid_listener.py does.

FLASK_SECRET_KEY / VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY / VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY: real secrets
(session signing key, Web Push signing key pair). Generate your own with
`python generate_vapid_keys.py` rather than reusing the placeholders
below — only the machine actually running app.py needs real values here.
"""

SMS_GATEWAY_IP = "0.0.0.0"
SMS_GATEWAY_PORT = "8080"

ROOMSYNC_SERVER_URL = "http://127.0.0.1:5000"

FLASK_SECRET_KEY = "change-me"
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY = "generate-your-own-with-generate_vapid_keys.py"
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY = "generate-your-own-with-generate_vapid_keys.py"
